(7289423, 1135893, 114285, '<td valign="top">When i first saw this, I thought ''OH MAN'', the roof is very similar to my entry, but this was a lot nicer.</td>', 'When i first saw this, I thought ''OH MAN'', the roof is very similar to my entry, but this was a lot nicer.', '2014-12-02 23:49:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(7289509, 1135944, 86218, '<td valign="top">Happy to give some feedback Don. <br/>A Gursky image no doubt and yet theres more. Sticking to the comp rules here Def helps to keep the image together yet also as mentioned in your note.. the style lends itself to breaking the mold and with focal point lacking and scattering you all over the scene yet contained and ordered with strong lines repeated. Cleverly done. The rythm generated from bottom to top gets broken by a pulse in the line running across the scene - the nets. One dont realise how much effect this has when viewing it. <br/> <br/>Exposure good and love the clouds and sky in this as well but with the birds confined to the ground. Im sure the Gursky effect would have been further enhanced if even the sky was scattered with birds. <br/>It''s Gursky..and yet you have thrown a different spin on it. Top contenders came in with copying textbook the style. Nice take on the challenge while generating an image which in your mind is Gursky.. yet stayed unique, different.<br/> <br/>Works for me<br/></td>', 'Happy to give some feedback Don. A Gursky image no doubt and yet theres more. Sticking to the comp rules here Def helps to keep the image together yet also as mentioned in your note.. the style lends itself to breaking the mold and with focal point lacking and scattering you all over the scene yet contained and ordered with strong lines repeated. Cleverly done. The rythm generated from bottom to top gets broken by a pulse in the line running across the scene - the nets. One dont realise how much effect this has when viewing it.  Exposure good and love the clouds and sky in this as well but with the birds confined to the ground. Im sure the Gursky effect would have been further enhanced if even the sky was scattered with birds. It''s Gursky..and yet you have thrown a different spin on it. Top contenders came in with copying textbook the style. Nice take on the challenge while generating an image which in your mind is Gursky.. yet stayed unique, different. Works for me', '2014-12-03 10:01:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(7289710, 1135607, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Like some of your commenters say, I too envy the fact that you *saw* this shot, and got it, and I didn''t :-/<br/> <br/>But the wide-angle length used, the repetition of sameness, coupled with perfect lighting and a subject most of us can relate to (I am wearing one of my many pairs of cheap reading glasses even as I write) make it a truly beguiling, and definitely Gursky-edque shot.  And look, you got an HM out of it, very well done in any challenge!<br/> <br/>Nitpicks...hmm sorry, but I  just can''t put on my Simon Cowell hat for this one.  Great dof, the utter simplicity and composition make it a shot well worth framing imnsho.<br/> <br/>Again well done, congrats on the HM and keep up the good work! :-)<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Like some of your commenters say, I too envy the fact that you *saw* this shot, and got it, and I didn''t :-/ But the wide-angle length used, the repetition of sameness, coupled with perfect lighting and a subject most of us can relate to (I am wearing one of my many pairs of cheap reading glasses even as I write) make it a truly beguiling, and definitely Gursky-edque shot.  And look, you got an HM out of it, very well done in any challenge! Nitpicks...hmm sorry, but I  just can''t put on my Simon Cowell hat for this one.  Great dof, the utter simplicity and composition make it a shot well worth framing imnsho. Again well done, congrats on the HM and keep up the good work! :-) Susan', '2014-12-03 19:26:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(7336811, 1135909, 93565, '<td valign="top">I missed this challenge during my hiatus. A pleasing shot in its own right, but very fitting for the challenge. Well done.</td>', 'I missed this challenge during my hiatus. A pleasing shot in its own right, but very fitting for the challenge. Well done.', '2015-04-02 15:16:47.000000', NULL, 0),
